Claude Official MCP Connector Requirements and Implementation Guide

1. Overview

This document summarizes the major requirements and implementation considerations for building an MCP server intended to work as an official/community Claude connector and potentially be submitted to Anthropic’s Claude Connectors Directory.

It covers:

* MCP server and transport requirements
* Authentication requirements
* Tool design requirements
* Tool annotations
* Error handling
* Security and privacy
* Testing and submission
* Source-code and GitHub requirements
* MCP tool-result size limits
* Claude Desktop vs. Claude Code limits
* Large-result handling
* Recommended architecture for data-heavy MCP servers

Important: MCP protocol compliance alone does not guarantee acceptance into Claude’s Connectors Directory. Anthropic applies additional functional, security, privacy, tool-design, and quality requirements.

⸻

