19. Retryability

Errors should ideally provide enough information for the client/model to determine whether retrying makes sense.

Example classification:

Error	Retry?
Invalid parameter	Usually no
Account not found	No, unless parameter changes
Authentication expired	Re-authentication required
Rate limited	Yes, after delay
Upstream timeout	Usually yes
Upstream 503	Usually yes
Internal transient failure	Possibly
Malformed JSON	No
Method not found	No

Do not blindly tell Claude to retry every error.

The error message should accurately reflect whether changing input, authenticating again, waiting, or retrying could resolve the issue.

