26. MCP Tool Result Size Limits

This is particularly important for data-heavy MCP servers.

Claude clients impose limits on how much MCP tool output can be handled in a single result.

The limits depend on the Claude environment.

A simplified comparison is:

Environment	Typical MCP result behavior
Claude.ai	Approximately 150,000 characters per large tool result
Claude Desktop	Approximately 150,000 characters per large tool result
Claude Code	Default token-based MCP output limit; configurable
Claude Code per-tool	Supports Anthropic-specific result-size metadata

These are tool-result handling limits, not necessarily the same as the model’s total context window.

⸻

27. Claude Desktop Result Limit

For Claude Desktop / Claude.ai, Anthropic documents handling around approximately:

150,000 characters

for an individual MCP tool result.

This is different from saying:

Claude only has a 150K-character context window.

It does not.

The limitation concerns how the Claude client handles individual MCP tool results.

⸻

28. Can the Claude Desktop Limit Be Increased?

Generally, no.

Anthropic does not currently document a supported Claude Desktop configuration allowing MCP developers/users to increase the approximately 150,000-character individual tool-result limit.

For example, there is no documented Claude Desktop equivalent of:

MAX_MCP_OUTPUT_TOKENS

that allows an MCP developer to simply configure:

150K
    |
    v
500K

for normal Claude Desktop connector operation.

Therefore:

Do NOT architect an official Claude connector around increasing
the Claude Desktop limit.

Instead, design the MCP API to return appropriately sized results.

⸻

29. Claude Code Is Different

Claude Code provides more control over MCP output limits.

For example:

export MAX_MCP_OUTPUT_TOKENS=50000

can increase the MCP output token threshold in Claude Code.

Claude Code also supports Anthropic-specific per-tool metadata such as:

{
  "_meta": {
    "anthropic/maxResultSizeChars": 200000
  }
}

Anthropic documents a maximum value for this mechanism of approximately:

500,000 characters

depending on the relevant Claude Code behavior/version.

This should not be confused with Claude Desktop.

Claude Code
    |
    +-- configurable MCP output behavior
Claude Desktop
    |
    +-- no equivalent documented developer setting
        for increasing the normal ~150K-character limit

⸻

30. Large API Responses

Suppose an upstream API returns:

Account A
    |
    +-- 2,000 holdings
    |
    +-- 40 fields per holding
Account B
    |
    +-- 3,000 holdings
    |
    +-- 40 fields per holding
Account C
    |
    +-- 4,000 holdings

Returning everything directly may produce:

500K characters
1M characters
2M characters
or more

Do not rely on Claude Desktop accepting the entire result.

