38. Avoid Excessive Tool Chaining

Do not force:

get_accounts
      |
      v
Claude guesses account
      |
      v
get_account_id
      |
      v
get_holdings
      |
      v
get_security
      |
      v
get_security_details

when a simpler interface could handle the request directly.

For example:

get_holdings(
    account_id=None,
    account_name=None,
    symbol=None,
    asset_type=None,
    fields=None,
    limit=100,
    cursor=None,
)

allows Claude to provide only the constraints available from the user’s request.

The goal is:

Minimize unnecessary orchestration
+
Minimize unnecessary data transfer

rather than optimizing only one of them.

