44. Recommended Internal Exception Structure

Conceptually:

class MCPApplicationError(Exception):
    pass
class ValidationFailedError(MCPApplicationError):
    pass
class UpstreamError(MCPApplicationError):
    pass
class InternalServiceError(MCPApplicationError):
    pass

Then at the MCP boundary:

try:
    result = service.execute(...)
except ValidationFailedError as exc:
    raise ToolError(
        f"Invalid request: {safe_message(exc)}"
    )
except UpstreamError:
    raise ToolError(
        "The requested service is temporarily unavailable. "
        "Please try again later."
    )
except Exception:
    request_id = generate_request_id()
    logger.exception(
        "Unexpected MCP tool failure",
        extra={"request_id": request_id}
    )
    raise ToolError(
        f"Unable to complete the request because of an internal "
        f"service error. Reference ID: {request_id}"
    )

The exact implementation depends on the FastMCP version and application architecture.

The important concept is:

Internal exception taxonomy
             |
             v
Central error mapper
             |
             v
Safe MCP-facing error

