Error Handling

Do not simply convert every error into ToolError.

Use:

Transport failure
    -> Transport error
MCP/JSON-RPC failure
    -> Protocol error
Authentication failure
    -> OAuth / HTTP error
Tool validation failure
    -> Tool execution error
Upstream dependency failure during tool execution
    -> Tool execution error
Unexpected tool runtime failure
    -> Sanitized tool execution error
       + detailed internal logging

FastMCP ToolError is a reasonable mechanism for normalizing tool-execution failures, but it should not replace the other error layers.

⸻

Claude Desktop MCP Result Limit

Claude Desktop / Claude.ai have approximately:

~150,000 characters

of practical individual MCP tool-result handling.

There is currently no documented supported configuration for simply increasing that limit in Claude Desktop.

⸻

Claude Code

Claude Code provides more configurable MCP output handling, including:

MAX_MCP_OUTPUT_TOKENS

and Anthropic-specific per-tool result-size metadata.

Do not assume those settings apply to Claude Desktop.

⸻

Large Data

Do not solve large MCP responses by trying to increase Claude Desktop’s limit.

Solve them through:

Filtering
+
Field projection
+
Pagination
+
Sorting
+
Server-side aggregation
+
On-demand detail retrieval

A good MCP tool should return:

the minimum amount of information necessary
to satisfy the current request

rather than:

all available information
and letting the LLM figure it out.

